# GitHub runner compose pool on pikachu. AppArmor is not required.
#
# Non-root runners (#292): the image ends as the base image runner account
# (uid 1001, gid 121) with RUN_AS_ROOT=false and NO passwordless sudo (the
# runner account is removed from the sudo group); the upstream entrypoint
# executes the CMD directly as that user. Toolchains live under /opt/rust
# (runner-owned) and /usr/local/go, not under /root.
#
# Deployment status (#292): the compose pool is not currently deployed
# (the operator retired it and no repo-level or gpu-h100 runners are
# registered; release.yml's live gate stays skipped until one is). This
# directory remains the fallback and GPU-gate definition; the next
# deployment must use this non-root image.
#
# Security boundary honesty (#292): job code in these containers runs
# non-root without passwordless sudo. The GPU service also mounts the host
# Docker socket, which is host-root-equivalent; for that service this is
# defense in depth, not a hard boundary.
#
# Layout:
#   ~/github-runners-bench-cli-compose   CI label bench-cli (this pool)
#   ~/github-runners-router-compose      CI label router
#   ~/github-runners-all-smi-compose     CI label all-smi
#   ~/github-runners-bench-cli           old bare-metal; docs-deploy stays here
#
# First time (once .env has RUNNER_TOKEN or ACCESS_TOKEN):
#   cd ~/github-runners-bench-cli-compose
# Bootstrap is managed by the runner host configuration; no repository shell bootstrap is provided.
#
# Non-root rollout (#292), once per host:
#   # 1. Set the host docker group id in .env before starting the GPU
#   #    service (required for the host Docker socket, uid 1001 cannot
#   #    otherwise use it):
#   #      echo "DOCKER_GID=$(getent group docker | cut -d: -f3)" >> .env
#   ./pool recreate
#   # 2. Pre-existing runner-tools named volumes keep their root-owned
#   #    content even after the image chowns /opt/hostedtoolcache, so drop
#   #    them once while the pool is stopped (they are only a tool cache;
#   #    `down -v` removes the project's named volumes):
#     docker compose down -v && ./pool start
#   # 3. Verify inside a running worker:
#   docker exec gha-bench-cli-1 id          # must print uid=1001(runner)
#   docker exec gha-bench-cli-1 cargo --version   # /opt/rust works non-root
#   docker exec gha-bench-cli-1 sudo -n true      # must FAIL: no passwordless sudo
#   docker exec gha-bench-cli-1 rustup show        # shared RUSTUP_HOME works
#   #    (GPU service: also verify `docker version` from inside the runner
#   #    with DOCKER_GID set, and keep untrusted fork PRs off that label.)
#
# Daily / manual:
#   ./pool start              # up -d
#   ./pool stop               # stop, keep containers
#   ./pool down               # remove containers
#   ./pool restart            # recreate whole pool
#   ./pool restart runner-1   # one worker
#   ./pool status
#   ./pool logs
#   ./pool logs runner-2
#   ./pool recreate           # rebuild image then recreate
#
# Optional systemd (boot start):
#   sudo cp gha-bench-cli-pool.service /etc/systemd/system/
#   sudo systemctl daemon-reload
#   sudo systemctl enable --now gha-bench-cli-pool
#   sudo systemctl restart gha-bench-cli-pool
#   sudo systemctl status gha-bench-cli-pool
#
# Do not attach bench-cli-docs-deploy to this pool.
#
# GPU runner (opt-in, label gpu-h100) for live-modality-smoke.yml:
#   The service runner-gpu sits behind compose profile `gpu`, so
#   `./pool start` never starts it. Host prerequisites:
#     - NVIDIA driver and NVIDIA Container Toolkit, with
#       `docker run --rm --gpus all nvidia/cuda:12.9.1-base-ubuntu24.04 nvidia-smi`
#       working on the host
#     - one H100 (or set GPU_LABELS to match what the host has)
#     - HF_CACHE_DIR (default /srv/hf-cache) created and writable; set the
#       repository variable LIVE_HF_HOME to the same path
#     - optional repository secret HF_TOKEN for gated models
#   Start / stop:
#     docker compose --profile gpu up -d runner-gpu
#     docker compose --profile gpu stop runner-gpu
#   Check passthrough from inside the runner:
#     docker exec gha-bench-cli-gpu nvidia-smi -L
#     docker exec gha-bench-cli-gpu docker version
#   How it works: the runner reserves the GPUs (so nvidia-smi can record
#   the SUT), mounts the host Docker socket, and uses host networking. The
#   cargo xtask serve starts vLLM / vllm-omni as sibling containers on the
#   host daemon with --gpus, publishes port 8000 on the host, and the smoke
#   step reaches them at 127.0.0.1:8000.
#   Security: the Docker socket is root on the host. Keep this runner on a
#   repo-scoped, ephemeral registration, and do not run untrusted fork PRs
#   on the gpu-h100 label (the live workflow has no pull_request trigger).
#   The GPU runner also carries the bench-cli label, so ordinary CI jobs can
#   land on it; drop bench-cli from GPU_LABELS to prevent that and change
#   runs-on in live-modality-smoke.yml to match.

